orming agent are equally open to web environment exploration, actively issuing environment-changing actions like click and type. Not surprisingly, the AGENTOCCAM + SteP Observation space example:</p></note></figure>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t<div type=\"references\">\n\n\t\t\t\t<listBibl>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b0\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<title level=\"m\" type=\"main\">Agent-e: From autonomous web navigation to foundational design principles in agentic systems</title>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Tamer</forename><surname>Abuelsaad</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Deepak</forename><surname>Akkil</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Prasenjit</forename><surname>Dey</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Ashish</forename><surname>Jagmohan</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Aditya</forename><surname>Vempaty</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Ravi</forename><surname>Kokku</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<ptr target=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.13032\" />\n\t\t<imprint>\n\t\t\t<date type=\"published\" when=\"2024\">2024</date>\n\t\t</imprint>\n\t</monogr>\n</biblStruct>\n\n<biblStruct status=\"extracted\" xml:id=\"b1\">\n\t<monogr>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Josh</forename><surname>Achiam</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Steven</forename><surname>Adler</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Sandhini</forename><surname>Agarwal</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persName><forename type=\"first\">Lama</forename><surname>Ahmad</surname></persName>\n\t\t</author>\n\t\t<author>\n\t\t\t<persNa